BINUTILSPROBE(1)

NAME
    binutilsprobe - test hosted GNU binutils round-trip behavior

SYNOPSIS
    /usr/libexec/tests/binutilsprobe

DESCRIPTION
    binutilsprobe is a guest regression probe for the staged GNU binutils
    tools. It writes a tiny assembly source and marker data file under /tmp,
    assembles the source with as, prepares an archive member, creates an
    archive with ar, indexes it with ranlib, links a generated i386 ELF with
    ld, and runs the resulting executable.

    The probe then checks the generated ELF with readelf, objdump, nm, size,
    strings, and addr2line. It also copies the ELF with objcopy, strips it
    with strip, and verifies that both transformed executables still run and
    print the stable marker:

        binutils roundtrip ok

    The probe is installed under /usr/libexec/tests and is normally run by the
    host-driven selftest suite rather than by hand. It is intended to validate
    the SmallOS-hosted binutils surface, not to replace the full upstream GNU
    binutils testsuite.

SEE ALSO
    selftest(1), tcc(1), shell(1)
